metadata:
  project: "RC Pop Star — Gyro Variant: Yokomo DP-302 V4"
  description: >-
    Channel map for the Yokomo DP-302 V4 gyro. More capable than the D-Box3 series:
    4 selectable modes (Normal/ASSIST × Hard/Soft gain), SBUS-based dual gain control,
    and an external LED status indicator output.

    Verified from: teamyokomo.com/downloadfiles/.../DP-302V4_User_manual.pdf
    (Scanned image PDF — read via Playwright browser screenshot, not pdftotext.)

    Connection diagram from the manual (English side):
      Receiver CH1 → gyro input (steering)
      Receiver CH2 → gyro input (optional, dual-gain or 2-channel mode)
      Receiver CH3 → gyro input (optional, 3-channel/SBUS mode)
      BATT          → gyro power from receiver/BEC
      Gyro output   → Servo
      LED output    → external LED indicator

    Dual gain (from manual): adjusted via gain channel of transmitter, "defaulted in S.BUS
    Mode." On the R7FG, S.BUS is output on CH7. Range: −100% to 0 (Hard Mode, red LED)
    and 0 to +100% (Soft Mode, green LED). Hard Mode recommended for most/beginners.

    Channel map with this gyro:
      CH1 (steering)  → DP-302 V4 CH1 + Killerbody 48102 CH1 (Y-cable)
      CH2 (throttle)  → XD10 Pro ESC + Killerbody 48102 CH2 (Y-cable)
      CH3 (VR knob)   → DP-302 V4 CH3 (optional — conflicts with R7FG default gyro CH3)
                        See note below about R7FG CH3 reassignment.
      CH4 (SwA)       → FREE
      CH5 (SwB)       → FREE
      CH6 (SwC/PPM)   → FREE
      CH7 (SwD/SBUS)  → DP-302 V4 gain (via S.BUS on CH7)

    R7FG CH3 conflict (from R7FG manual):
      R7FG built-in gyro sensitivity defaults to CH3 (VR knob).
      DP-302 V4 optionally uses CH3 as a 3rd gain channel.
      Resolution: disable R7FG built-in gyro (factory default = OFF) and assign CH3
      to the DP-302 V4 gain, OR leave CH3 unused and use CH7/SBUS for dual gain instead.

    R7FG built-in gyro conflict:
      Same as D-Box3 variants: leave R7FG gyro OFF (factory default). Two gyros on CH1
      simultaneously = oscillation. From R7FG manual (radiolink.com/rc6gsv3_manual):
      "Factory setting is gyro function OFF by default."

    Specs from teamyokomo.com product page:
      AMain p6011743 $75.99. 4 selectable modes. SW1: Normal/ASSIST. SW2: Normal/Reverse.

# TODO:
#   [ ] Decide: use CH3+CH7 for dual gain control, or just CH7/SBUS alone?
#   [ ] Run END POINT (servo stroke) setup: hold SW + power on → rotate to limits
#   [ ] Verify SW2 direction (Normal vs Reverse) with test steer before driving
#   [ ] If CH3 used for DP-302 gain: set R7FG GYRO menu to STD mode to free CH3

connectors:

  R7FG_RX:
    type: "Radiolink R7FG receiver"
    subtype: "7-channel, 2.4GHz; CH7/SBUS used for DP-302 V4 dual gain"
    pincount: 7
    pinlabels:
      - "CH1 SIG (steering)"
      - "CH1 VCC (from XD10 BEC)"
      - "CH1 GND"
      - "CH2 SIG (throttle)"
      - "CH2 GND"
      - "CH3 SIG (optional: DP-302 gain or free)"
      - "CH7/SBUS (S.BUS output for DP-302 dual gain)"
    notes: >
      R7FG manual: radiolink.com.cn/download/3edba11a28636d2f5f2f6002d04a92aa.pdf
      R7FG built-in gyro = OFF (factory default) — must stay OFF with external gyro.
      CH7 outputs S.BUS when S.BUS mode enabled (short press binding button once).
      LED indicator: Green=PWM, Blue=SBUS, Red=Gyro mode, Purple=Gyro+SBUS.
      BEC supply from XD10 Pro ESC.

  XD10_ESC:
    type: "Hobbywing XD10 Pro ESC"
    subtype: "BEC 5–7.4V adjustable (item 1G), sensored brushless"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels:
      - "TH SIG (throttle, plugs into receiver TH=CH2)"
      - "BEC VCC (5–7.4V out to receiver and servos)"
      - "GND"
    notes: >
      Manual: hobbywing.com/en/uploads/file/20221012/7cb44bc6cf370ca8bb8ac96c29b6a7e3.pdf
      BEC: "adjustable from 5V to 7.4V (step: 0.1V)" per features list.
      Do NOT connect separate BEC to receiver.

  GYRO_DP302V4:
    type: "Yokomo DP-302 V4 drift gyro"
    subtype: "4-mode: Normal/ASSIST × Hard/Soft gain. SBUS dual gain."
    pincount: 6
    pinlabels:
      - "CH1 in (steering, from receiver via Y-cable)"
      - "CH2 in (optional gain/2-ch mode)"
      - "CH3 in (optional 3-ch gain — see R7FG CH3 conflict note)"
      - "BATT (VCC/GND from receiver BEC)"
      - "Servo out (corrected steering to servo)"
      - "LED out (status LED, external)"
    notes: >
      Manual: teamyokomo.com/downloadfiles/.../DP-302V4_User_manual.pdf (scanned image PDF)
      SW1: up=Normal, down=ASSIST (default=Normal).
      SW2: Normal/Reverse servo direction.
      Dual gain via S.BUS (CH7 on R7FG): −100%→0 = Hard Mode (red LED, beginners);
      0→+100% = Soft Mode (green LED, expert). Hard Mode recommended to start.
      LED status: Red fast flash=initializing; Green fast=signal loss; Red solid=Normal gain;
      Green solid=AVCS gain; Yellow slow=stroke setting; Off=0% gain.

  KB48102_LED:
    type: "Killerbody 48102 LED control box"
    subtype: "Reads CH1 steering (Y) + CH2 throttle (Y). Not all radios compatible."
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels:
      - "CH1 in (steering sense, via Y-cable)"
      - "CH2 in (throttle sense, via Y-cable)"
      - "VCC/GND (from receiver BEC)"
    notes: >
      KB48102 instruction sheet: killerbodyrc.com/Prod_image/instructions/48102.PDF
      Bench-test R7FG compatibility before permanent install.

  SERVO_ST:
    type: "Steering servo (driven by DP-302 V4 output)"
    pincount: 3
    pinlabels: ["SIG (from gyro)", "VCC", "GND"]

cables:

  W_CH1_Y:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [WH, RD, BK]
    wirelabels: ["CH1 SIG", "VCC", "GND"]
    length: 0.15 m
    notes: "Y-cable: receiver CH1 → DP-302 V4 CH1 + Killerbody CH1."

  W_CH2_Y:
    wirecount: 2
    colors: [WH, BK]
    wirelabels: ["CH2 SIG", "GND"]
    length: 0.15 m
    notes: "Y-cable: receiver CH2 → XD10 ESC + Killerbody CH2."

  W_ESC_TH:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [WH, RD, BK]
    wirelabels: ["TH SIG", "BEC VCC", "GND"]
    length: 0.2 m
    notes: "XD10 Pro throttle + BEC cable to receiver CH2."

  W_GYRO_SERVO:
    wirecount: 3
    colors: [WH, RD, BK]
    wirelabels: ["SIG (corrected)", "VCC", "GND"]
    length: 0.15 m
    notes: "DP-302 V4 servo output to steering servo."

  W_CH7_SBUS:
    wirecount: 1
    colors: [OG]
    wirelabels: ["SBUS (dual gain)"]
    length: 0.2 m
    notes: "CH7 S.BUS output from R7FG to DP-302 V4 CH3 input for dual gain control."

connections:

  - - XD10_ESC: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_ESC_TH: [1, 2, 3]
    - R7FG_RX: [4, 2, 5]

  - - R7FG_RX: [1, 2, 3]
    - W_CH1_Y: [1, 2, 3]
    - GYRO_DP302V4: [1, 4, 4]

  - - W_CH1_Y: [1, 2, 3]
    - KB48102_LED: [1, 3, 3]

  - - R7FG_RX: [4, 5]
    - W_CH2_Y: [1, 2]
    - KB48102_LED: [2, 3]

  - - GYRO_DP302V4: [5, 4, 4]
    - W_GYRO_SERVO: [1, 2, 3]
    - SERVO_ST: [1, 2, 3]

  - - R7FG_RX: [7]
    - W_CH7_SBUS: [1]
    - GYRO_DP302V4: [3]
